        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Tom took over the second half of Path-210 and greatly enhanced my understanding of the global context in which the HIV/AIDS pandemic took place.\nGreat class, engaging lectures, and very insightful and established professors. Exams are straightforward, but the grade is made up of only three + attendance points, so be sure to study. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Great professor and Path Bio 210 was a great class; I would highly recommend him and Dave!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "He teaches Path210 with Dave, and they were the best! Super well establised in their field, class had some scientific content but very accessible for even non-STEM majors. The course is super up-to-date and very interesting. A few reading for every class, and graded based on attendance and 3 midterms. Great class for new UW students. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "PATH210 is an honors only course which was nice because the class was very small and the lectures were more like discussions. It wasn't a very difficult course (one of the less sciencey bio credits), but the only things scored were the 3 multiple choice exams, so it was important to study for those. Both Tom and Dave were great professors overall.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            }
